    # Note: The problem uses 1-based indexing for description, but we'll use 0-based for implementation.
    # The rule is: combine i and j -> A[i][j] if i >= j, else A[j][i].
    # In the input, the row i (0-indexed) contains A_{i+1, 1}, A_{i+1, 2}, ..., A_{i+1, N+1}
    # Wait, the input format says:
    # A_{1,1}
    # A_{2,1} A_{2,2}
    # ...
    # A_{N,1} ... A_{N,N}
    # So row i (0-indexed) corresponds to element i+1.
    # The values in row i are A_{i+1, 1}, A_{i+1, 2}, ..., A_{i+1, N}.
